<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#commentsOn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates a social-media comment to the post it replies to. Recruiter replies in comment threads are modelled because in the Colmex corpus the recruitment contact is frequently made there rather than in the post itself."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#ForeignLanguageTeacherScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The candidate is offered a teaching position abroad (typically Spanish in Asia or English in Latin America) with housing, visa and flight paid by the agency. On arrival the promised contract does not exist: the candidate is placed in a different role, forced to pay back 'travel expenses', has documents retained, or finds the school is a front for sex tourism or forced domestic work. Documented corridors include Mexico-China, Mexico-Korea, and Peru-Japan."@en .
