<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#BeggingRingScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Offer of 'help' or 'a job in the city' that leads to forced begging under the control of a ring leader. Common victims are minors, persons with disabilities, and migrants with precarious status. The ring leader confiscates earnings and controls movement. Named explicitly in the UNODC Protocol against Trafficking in Persons glossary and discussed by UNICEF in urban contexts in Mexico, Honduras and Guatemala. Maps to :PurposeForcedLabour or :PurposeSlavery depending on the context."@en .
