<https://w3id.org/ratr-o> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "v1.9 (3 Nov 2026): persistent namespace moved to https://w3id.org/ratr-o (previous IRIs under ramona.ai were placeholders on a domain not controlled by the project). Adds the social-media criminal-recruitment module derived from El Colegio de Mexico (2025), Del scroll al jale. v1.9.1: in the OWL 2 QL profile under the OWL API checker (ROBOT 1.9.11); 16 data ranges outside the QL datatype map moved to rdfs:Literal; consistent under HermiT with and without data. See docs/validation/VALIDATION_REPORT.md. v1.10: real press offer corpus (data/real/press_offers.csv); Type A and Type B red-flag classes, criminal-recruitment offers and offer provenance. v1.10.1, v1.10.2 and v1.10.3: three audit passes before the delivery of O1, which found and fixed nineteen defects. The third pass executed the 40 reference queries and the seed files for the first time rather than reading them; see docs/AUDIT_O1_SUMMARY.md and docs/validation/QUERY_EXECUTION_REPORT.md. v1.10.3 restores the eight skos:closeMatch alignments to HUTRO with IRIs verified one by one in the BioPortal concept browser on 10 November 2026."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#TypeOfExploitation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Close match to the HUTRO concept 'type of exploitation' (Human Trafficking Ontology, Danial Zemchal Tesfahans, BioPortal submission 1 of 22 April 2025, status alpha, SKOS format). The concept IRI was verified on 10 November 2026 in the BioPortal concept browser, which reports it as the concept Id and resolves it to the preferred label 'Type of exploitation'. HUTRO concepts are skos:Concept instances that also carry owl:NamedIndividual, so the match is recorded as an annotation assertion on this class rather than as an OWL object-property assertion, which keeps the ontology inside the OWL 2 QL profile."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#AgeGroup> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grupo etario"@es .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#MeansFraud> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Fraude"@es .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#hasEvidenceSource> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Provenance, stated without restricting the kind of thing being traced. Routes, victim records, patterns and offers all carry at least one evidence source, so this property has a range but no domain, and the kind-specific properties :derivedFrom (patterns) and :offerDocumentedIn (offers) are subproperties of it. A query that asks what any fact rests on uses this property; a query about one kind of fact uses the subproperty."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#datasetName> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
