<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#GigEconomyFakeDriverScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The candidate is offered work as a ride-hailing or delivery driver for a platform (Uber, DiDi, Cabify, Beat, Rappi, DiDi Food). The recruiter provides a 'rented' vehicle on terms that include daily rent, insurance fees and maintenance charges. The arithmetic guarantees the driver ends each week in deficit, binding them through accumulating debt. The vehicle is often stolen or fraudulently registered and is used to extract labour under the threat of criminal complaint."@en .
