<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#ExploitationRisk> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Risk that the offer leads to substandard working conditions, wage theft, excessive hours or other exploitation that does not rise to the legal definition of trafficking."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#ForcedCriminalityScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Offer advertised as 'private security', 'bodyguard', 'armed escort', 'watchman at a ranch' or 'warehouse security' with atypically high salary. The real purpose is enlistment into organised-crime armed structures, most notably as halcones, sicarios, or coca-processing labour. Archetypal Mexican case: the CJNG Rancho Izaguirre (Teuchitlán, Jalisco) recruiting scheme of 2024-2025."@en .
