<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#victimMaritalStatus> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "ICS-TIP additional disaggregating variable. Controlled vocab: single, married, cohabiting, separated, divorced, widowed, unknown."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#audioDescription> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "descripción del audio"@es .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#pctOfCases> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal> .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#agentName> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Name of the agent as it appears in the offer or the report. For recruiters this is the name they gave, which is frequently false, and never a verified identity."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#RecruitmentPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Patrón de reclutamiento"@es .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#InPersonLureScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The offer exists solely to bring the candidate to a physical location under the appearance of a hiring event or interview. The real purpose is kidnapping, assault, sexual violence or femicide. Characterised by plausible role, nameless company, multi-use building address, request to come alone and without identification. Documented archetypal case: Edith Guadalupe Valdez Saldívar, Benito Juárez CDMX, April 2026."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#victimMaritalStatus> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#PalermoPurpose> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The PURPOSE element of the Palermo Protocol Article 3(a): 'for the purpose of exploitation', which the Protocol exemplifies as 'the exploitation of the prostitution of others or other forms of sexual exploitation, forced labour or services, slavery or practices similar to slavery, servitude or the removal of organs'."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#exhibitsMeans> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#historicalOfferCount> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "historical offer count"@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#offerVerbatimQuote> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/ratr-o#JobOffer> .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#countryName> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "nombre del país"@es .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#MeansPaymentOrBenefit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#CriminalRecruitmentOffer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Criminal recruitment offer"@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#DocumentationType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/HUTROdocumentation_type> .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#DirectRecruitmentPost> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Condition NR of Colmex 2025: the post explicitly invites the audience to join a criminal group (e.g. 'Quieres jale? Todavia hay plazas', 'seguimos con el reclutamiento activo'). Such a post is a job offer, and every such offer exhibits some forced-criminality scheme (existential axiom, allowed on the right-hand side in OWL 2 QL)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#offerOutcome> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Controlled vocabulary: rescate, desaparicion, explotacion_sexual, explotacion_laboral, fraude_economico, homicidio, detencion_reclutador, other."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#routeDominantExploitation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The single exploitation type attested for the majority of victims on this route."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#lexiconIsVerbatim> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "textual de la fuente"@es .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#OrganRemovalRecruitmentScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://www.unodc.org/documents/human-trafficking/2015/UNODC_Assessment_Toolkit_TIP_for_the_Purpose_of_Organ_Removal.pdf> .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#flagKeywordPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/ratr-o#RedFlag> .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#WomenInvitationSignal> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#SurvivorTestimonyPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "95 patterns in the seeds. 88 carry one of six kind values: classic_a (5), credible_b (7), communication (7), recruitment (9), exploitation (10), deep_textual (50); 7 carry none. Five of the six kinds have a subclass here; deep_textual has none and is read off :patternHasKind. Counted against the seed files on 10 November 2026."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#exhibitsPurpose> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
