<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#hasVulnerabilityFactor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/ratr-o#DemographicProfile> .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#MeansAbuseOfVulnerability> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The MEANS 'abuse of a position of vulnerability' in the sense of Palermo Protocol Article 3(a). In Ramona's corpus the vulnerability most often invoked is unemployment or urgent need of income, which is why :VulnerabilityFactor is modelled separately on the demographic profile."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#FraudScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "26 subclasses in all, 21 of them direct. 15 are attested in the verified press corpus; the rest are declared for schemes documented in official sources but not yet matched by a row. Counted against the ontology and the seed files on 10 November 2026."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#CommunicationPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/ratr-o#SurvivorTestimonyPattern> .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#Transfer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The ACT of transfer in the sense of Palermo Protocol Article 3(a): handing control over the person from one party to another."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#BeggingRingScheme> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#CriminalRecruitmentOffer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/ratr-o#JobOffer> .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#tipEventHasMeans> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates a TIP event to one of its Palermo Means. ICS-TIP requires at least one means per adult-victim event."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#offerIsActive> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Whether the offer was still reachable at the time of the last check."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#Victim> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Victim records come from CTDC v2025 (the IOM differential-privacy synthetic release) and from anonymised press case references, loaded by scripts/ingest_ctdc.py. The seed files in db/ create the victim tables but populate none of them, because the CTDC release is not redistributed in this repository. Until that script is run the 18 victim mappings produce nothing and the queries that rest on them return no rows; docs/MAPPING_COVERAGE.md lists which."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#Submission> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Submission"@en .
