<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#evidenceArchivedUrl> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "evidence archived URL (e.g. archive.today)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#PalermoMeans> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Eight canonical sub-concepts from Article 3(a)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#MLMHealthBeautyScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A multi-level marketing operation centred on nutritional supplements, cosmetics, slimming products or wellness programmes. Presented as an employment or business opportunity, in practice the participant earns only by recruiting further 'distributors' and by purchasing inventory that cannot be sold on the open market. Canonical examples in Latin America include product lines marketed through Facebook groups and WhatsApp chains."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#Country> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A country or territory used as the origin, destination, stopover or jurisdiction of an offer, a route, a platform, a recruiter or a TIP event. Identified by its ISO 3166-1 code through :countryISOCode."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#PalermoAction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://www.ohchr.org/en/instruments-mechanisms/instruments/protocol-prevent-suppress-and-punish-trafficking-persons> .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#NationalReachSignal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Recruits from anywhere in the country ('todo Mexico'). Colmex 2025, image 10."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#FakeMaquilaScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Offer of employment at an export-processing factory in the Mexican north border or in border free-trade zones. The maquila is either non-existent (workers arrive to find no facility), a cover for forced labour in a related industry (for example drug packaging, human-trafficking logistics), or a real facility operating under abusive conditions below the legal minimum. Candidates commonly relocate from southern Mexico and Central America."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#schemeTargetsAgeGroup> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates a fraud scheme to the age group it preferentially targets."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#InPersonLureScheme> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#ForcedChildMarriageScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Checked 10 November 2026: the oaxaca.gob.mx page returns HTTP 500. The Internet Archive snapshot of 24 February 2025 is cited alongside it."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#languageName> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Name of the language in English."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#MinorAgeMentionSignal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The item mentions an age under 18 ('puedo entrar con 16'). Colmex 2025, image 22. Links the item to child recruitment."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#tipEventInvolves> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/ratr-o#Victim> .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#SportsTalentScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://fifpro.org/en/supporting-players/safe-working-environments/human-trafficking/> .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#TraffickingRisk> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#AgriculturalBondageScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Offer of seasonal agricultural work (jornalero, harvest, produce packing) that leads to wage theft, deductions for housing and food that exceed the wage, confiscation of identification documents, and restriction of movement through geographic isolation. Documented by ILO, UNODC and the Polaris Project in the US-Mexico corridor (fresh produce, coffee, tomato) and in internal Mexican migration from southern states to Sinaloa, Sonora and Baja California. The CTDC dataset registers agricultural labour as a distinct exploitation subtype."@en .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty> .
