<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#GangRecruitmentSchoolsScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Specific subtype of child recruitment where the entry point is the school ground or school exit. Recruiters are often students slightly older than the target or adults posing as relatives. Common in Central America (MS-13, Barrio 18) and in Mexican states with heavy cartel presence (Michoacán, Guerrero, Jalisco, Tamaulipas). The Gobierno de Zapopan published a public prevention programme in 2026. The Ramona press corpus holds 26 items from REDIM's data and advocacy blog (count recomputed 10 November 2026 from data/processed/press_summary.json)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#candidateDefraudedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/ratr-o#Candidate> .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#PalermoPurpose> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Finalidad (Palermo)"@es .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#offerPayAmount> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Pay amount stated in the offer."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#vulnerabilityFactorName> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "vulnerability factor name"@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#ChildRecruitmentCriminalScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/ratr-o#ForcedCriminalityScheme> .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#CommunicationPattern> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#contactHash> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SHA-256 digest of the recruiter's contact identifier. The digest lets the same contact be recognised across reports without storing the phone number or the account name."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#VulnerabilityFactor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Vulnerability factor"@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#hasEvidenceSource> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/ratr-o#EvidenceSource> .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#transportedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates a victim to the means of transportation used to move them."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#visualDescription> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "visual description"@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#offerDocumentedIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/ratr-o#EvidenceSource> .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#CriminalCultureExaltationPost> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Criminal-culture exaltation post (ECC)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#MeansDeception> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The MEANS 'deception' in the sense of Palermo Protocol Article 3(a). A job offer whose terms misrepresent the role, the pay, the employer or the place of work realises this means."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#audioDescription> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Description of the audio track of the post, including the song used. The audio is recorded because in the Colmex corpus the belico soundtrack is part of what makes the post legible as a recruitment post."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#PrivateChannelCallSignal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Redirects the audience to a private message ('escribe al privado', 'manda DM'). Colmex 2025, images 10, 13, 14, 19, 21."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#victimOfExploitation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "victim of exploitation type"@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#transportedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/ratr-o#TransportationMeans> .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#TIPEvent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A trafficking-in-persons event as defined by the International Classification Standard for Administrative Data on Trafficking in Persons (ICS-TIP, IOM and UNODC, 2023). The TIP event is the central unit of classification in ICS-TIP. In RATR-O a TIPEvent aggregates one victim with at least one Palermo Action, at least one Palermo Means, and at least one Palermo Purpose."@en .
