<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#FamilyAppealSignal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Frames joining as sacrifice for the family ('que harias por tu mama', 'sacar a mi jefita adelante'). Colmex 2025, pp. 23 and 51."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#recruitmentMethodName> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Controlled vocabulary: personal_network, false_job_offer, social_media_contact, abduction, sale_by_family, debt_bondage, other."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#documentationTypeName> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "nombre del tipo de documentación"@es .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#CommunicationTool> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Close match to the HUTRO concept 'smuggler and trafficker communication tools' (Human Trafficking Ontology, Danial Zemchal Tesfahans, BioPortal submission 1 of 22 April 2025, status alpha, SKOS format). The concept IRI was verified on 10 November 2026 in the BioPortal concept browser, which reports it as the concept Id and resolves it to the preferred label 'Smuggler and Trafficker Communication Tools'. HUTRO concepts are skos:Concept instances that also carry owl:NamedIndividual, so the match is recorded as an annotation assertion on this class rather than as an OWL object-property assertion, which keeps the ontology inside the OWL 2 QL profile. HUTRO omits the conjunction in the local name. Versions up to 1.10 of this file used smuggler_and_trafficker_communication_tools, which does not resolve."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#ClassicRedFlagPattern> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#offerScreenshotUrl> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "URL of the stored screenshot of the offer. Screenshots are kept because deceptive offers are typically deleted by the recruiter within days."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#patternName> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Short name of the survivor-testimony pattern."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#MeansDeception> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Deception"@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#DominanceBucket> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A qualitative frequency band used to describe how often a pattern is observed in the observatory corpus: hot is at least 5 percent of cases, warm is 1 to 5 percent, cold is below 1 percent. The band is a class with one individual per value so that a query can group patterns by band; :dominanceBucketValue carries the same information as a literal for clients that do not traverse the object property."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ratr-o#documentationTypeName> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "documentation type name"@en .
